  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The temperature of an ideal gas is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. If r.m.s. speed of gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. Then, r.m.s. speed of the gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> will be:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "IclBl",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "H6ZMh",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
